any push or remote.

## Pipeline

Each stage runs as its workflow says (`workflows/NN-*.md` in the exam-prep skill). This table holds
only this course's choices. Waves run parallel inside and sequential across; each agent writes one
new file; the main session merges single-threaded. Load the delegation skill before the first
spawn, and spawn unnamed.

| Stage | Who | This course | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| 01 ingest | main | {{ADAPTERS: PDF, reveal.js HTML, ebook, Ed}} | `MANIFEST.md` counts, renders, Ed digest |
| 02 extract | {{N}} agents | {{DECK SPLITS: one whole deck per agent; decks over P pages split at a section divider, 3-page overlap}} | `_build/extract/<doc>.md` |
| 03 backbone | main | {{EXPECTED SECTIONS, final cut set by the extracts}} | `_build/backbone.md` |
| 04 write | {{N}} writers | one per backbone section | `notes/NN-<slug>.md` |
| 05 verify | main, {{N}} section reviewers, {{N}} checklist auditors | | fixes applied single-threaded |
| 06 site | {{N}} converters, then main | | the notes page |
| 07 cheat sheet | {{main or 1 agent}} | {{ONLY IF ALLOWED}} | `cheatsheet/` |
| 08 practice | {{N}} agents, then 1 cold solver | {{QUESTION SHAPES}} | `practice/` |

`pending` rows of `MANIFEST.md` are checked at every stage boundary: one that has arrived is
ingested and extracted before stage 03 runs, or before the next stage when 03 is done.

## Rules the build follows

- Pedagogy and wording: `_build/STYLE.md`. The look: `_build/CHASSIS.md`. Markdown to HTML:
  `_build/CONVERT.md`. All three are this hub's copies of the skill's templates, baseline
  {{BASELINE_DATE}}.
- Cross-references: the id registry in `_build/backbone.md`, fixed before any writer starts.
- The mock page has three views (by paper, by question type, by topic), so every question part is
  tagged with its type and its topic.

Checked before approval: visual design, pedagogy and wording, structure and enumeration,
cross-references, the mock views and the checker each name the rule above that governs them.

